    content: "---\nname: android-compose-jni\ndescription: Architect and optimize 120fps Android apps across Kotlin, Jetpack Compose, and zero-panic Rust JNI native cores.\nwhen_not_to_use: Web-only Svelte/CSS tasks, CI YAML debugging (use github-apk-ci-debugger), or Termux shell ops.\nverified: \"2026-11\"\ntriggers: [kotlin, compose, 120fps, jni, ffi, rust-jni, unwrap, sigabrt]\n---\n# Android Compose & Rust JNI Architect (v6)\n\n## Must-do\n- **Compose 120fps:** Annotate UI state with `@Immutable`/`@Stable`; wrap unstable collections or use `kotlinx.collections.immutable`.\n- **Defer State Reads:** Read fast-changing scroll/gesture/animation states inside lambda modifiers (`Modifier.offset { ... }`, `Modifier.graphicsLayer { ... }`), never in `@Composable` bodies.\n- **Streaming Lists & Radius:** Use stable `key = { it.id }` in `LazyColumn`, isolate active token streaming into a leaf composable, and clamp animated radii with `.coerceAtLeast(0.dp)`.\n- **Thread & Zero-Panic JNI (`lib*.so`):** Never run synchronous JNI, file I/O, or parsing on `Dispatchers.Main` (use `IO`/`Default`). Wrap `#[no_mangle] pub extern \"C\"` entry points in `Result` + `std::panic::catch_unwind` returning structured error codes; release `JNIEnv` local refs cleanly.\n\n## Verification Gate & Invariants\n- Verify 1:1 JNI signatures (`Java_pkg_Class_method` vs `external fun`), grep FFI entry files for `.unwrap()`/`.expect()` (-> 0 hits), and run `./gradlew compileDebugKotlin` or `cargo check --target aarch64-linux-android`.\n- **NEVER** allow `.unwrap()`/`.expect()` in JNI entry points or claim 120fps without Android GPU Profiler/Perfetto evidence.\n",
