    content: "---\nname: code-review\ndescription: Audit completed git diffs before commit/merge for spec drift, security/concurrency hazards, and UI/build regressions with file:line fixes.\nwhen_not_to_use: Initial crash/log triage before a patch exists (use triage) or greenfield architecture planning.\nverified: \"2026-11\"\ntriggers: [git diff, pr review, pre-merge, staged diff, regression audit]\n---\n# Code Review (v6 · Pre-Merge Diff Auditor)\n\n## Must-do\n1. **Scope Diff Safely (100K-Safe):** Run `git diff --stat` first, then inspect code hunks excluding lockfiles/bundles (`git diff -- . ':(exclude)*lock*' ':(exclude)dist/*'`). Cross-check every hunk against `spec.md` (if present).\n2. **Risk Checklist:**\n   - `[P0]` Secret leaks, injection/auth flaws, Rust `.unwrap()` across JNI, infinite loops, broken check/build, or stripped prod CSS (e.g., lost `backdrop-filter`).\n   - `[P1]` IO/coroutine races, Compose recomposition storms, Svelte 4 legacy syntax, WCAG AA/A11y regressions (`inert`/focus/ARIA), `375px` overflow, tap `<44px`.\n   - `[P2]` Scope drift, dead code, files `>350` lines (`>300` for UI components).\n3. **Output Contract:** State verdict (`APPROVE` / `REQUEST CHANGES`) + findings ordered `P0 -> P2` with exact `file:line`, impact, and concrete replacement code.\n\n## Invariants\n- **NEVER** dump lockfiles, `dist/`, or binary diffs into context; **NEVER** cite unread files or guessed line numbers.\n- **NEVER** auto-edit files during a review unless explicitly asked to apply fixes.\n",
