    kind: "skill",
    tags: ['skill', 'library'],
    content: "---\nname: db-optimizer\ndescription: Optimize SQLite, Postgres, and Supabase schemas, B-tree indexes, WAL concurrency, and query plans verified via EXPLAIN.\nwhen_not_to_use: In-memory UI state, shell scripts, or non-database file operations.\nverified: \"2026-11\"\ntriggers: [sqlite, postgres, supabase, index, explain query plan, wal, n+1, rls]\n---\n# DB Optimizer (v6 · Verified Query & Index Tuning)\n\n## Must-do\n1. **B-Tree Index Design:** Place equality columns (`=`) first, then choose the next column intentionally for either **Range selectivity** (`<, >, BETWEEN`) OR **Sort elimination** (`ORDER BY ... LIMIT`) — never assume `(eq, sort, range)` gives a B-tree seek on `range`. Index columns referenced in Postgres/Supabase RLS `USING` policies.\n2. **SQLite Android/Termux Tuning:** On connection init set `PRAGMA journal_mode=WAL;`, `PRAGMA synchronous=NORMAL;`, `PRAGMA foreign_keys=ON;`, and `PRAGMA busy_timeout=5000;` to prevent `SQLITE_BUSY` under concurrent reads/writes.\n3. **Kill N+1 & Full Scans:** Replace query loops with `JOIN`, `IN`, or batched `INSERT/UPSERT` inside a single transaction; paginate with keyset (`WHERE id > ?`) instead of large `OFFSET`.\n\n## Verification Gate & Invariants\n- Capture before/after `EXPLAIN QUERY PLAN` (SQLite) or `EXPLAIN (ANALYZE, BUFFERS)` (Postgres) proving `SEARCH ... USING INDEX` / Index Scan replaces `SCAN TABLE` / Seq Scan.\n- **NEVER** add indexes blindly without weighing write amplification, or claim latency improvements without actual `EXPLAIN` output.\n",
