    content: "---\nname: implement-spec\ndescription: Execute an approved spec.md bottom-up in dependency order with milestone checks, zero scope drift, and verified acceptance proof.\nwhen_not_to_use: Exploratory debugging without a spec (use diagnosing-bugs) or open-ended brainstorming.\nverified: \"2026-11\"\ntriggers: [execute spec.md, bottom-up build, acceptance criteria, approved spec]\n---\n# Implement Spec (v6 · Bottom-Up Spec Executor)\n\n## Must-do\n1. **Parse & Lock Scope:** Read `spec.md` (and `handoff.md` if resuming) to extract file map, contracts, edge cases, and acceptance checks before editing.\n2. **Build Bottom-Up:** Execute strictly in order: `Types/Models -> Core Domain / Rust FFI -> IO/Network -> UI -> Tests`. Run a targeted compile/check after every layer.\n3. **Drift & Blocker Policy:** Keep edits strictly inside `spec.md` files (no mid-flight unrelated refactors). If a platform constraint contradicts `spec.md`, pause, update `spec.md` minimally, then resume. Cap retries at **2 attempts** on external blockers (env/403/missing tool), then stop and report `Blocked`.\n4. **Verification Gate:** Cross-check every `spec.md` acceptance criterion with concrete passing command output (`pnpm run check && pnpm run build`, tests, `git status`). If work spans sessions, write a compact `handoff.md`.\n\n## Invariants\n- **NEVER** mark complete with `TODO` stubs, skipped edge-case fallbacks, or unexecuted verification checks.\n- **NEVER** fabricate passing output or loop blindly past 2 failed attempts on the same blocker.\n",
