    kind: "skill",
    tags: ['skill', 'library'],
    content: "---\nname: to-tickets\ndescription: Split spec.md into atomic, DAG-ordered vertical tickets with disjoint ownedFiles and runnable done-checks for sequential or /swarm runs.\nwhen_not_to_use: Single-file fixes that do not need multi-step slicing or parallel worker coordination.\nverified: \"2026-11\"\ntriggers: [break into tickets, parallel tasks, sprint slices, swarm tickets]\n---\n# To-Tickets (v6 · Atomic DAG Slicer)\n\n## Must-do\n1. **Vertical Slicing:** Each ticket delivers one testable vertical slice (`1-3` files, `<300` lines net diff) with explicit `ownedFiles`.\n2. **Disjoint Ownership & Fan-In:** Parallel tickets MUST have zero overlapping `ownedFiles`. Defer shared manifests/entries (`package.json`, `build.gradle.kts`, `AndroidManifest.xml`, `AGENTS.md`, JNI bridges) to the final single-owner integration ticket.\n3. **Compact Ticket Schema:**\n   - `[T-01] <Imperative deliverable>` | `Depends On:` `None` / `[T-0X]`\n   - `Owned Files:` exact file paths\n   - `Done-Check:` exact runnable command (`pnpm run check && pnpm run build`, `./gradlew test`, `cargo test`, `curl`, `node --test`)\n4. **Pre-Output Gate:** Verify the dependency graph is acyclic (valid DAG) and `ownedFiles` across every parallel wave are strictly disjoint.\n\n## Invariants\n- **NEVER** emit vague tickets (\"Setup backend\", \"Polish UI\") lacking exact file paths and a runnable done-check.\n- **NEVER** allow two parallel tickets to edit the same file.\n",
