    kind: "skill",
    tags: ['skill', 'library'],
    content: "---\nname: wizard\ndescription: Guide multi-step setups, migrations, and deployments with Termux-safe copy-paste commands, observable checks, and 1-line recovery.\nwhen_not_to_use: Code architecture design, diff auditing (use code-review), or single-command lookups.\nverified: \"2026-11\"\ntriggers: [step-by-step setup, onboarding guide, install walkthrough, migration steps]\n---\n# Wizard (v6 · Mobile-Safe Guided Ops)\n\n## Must-do\n1. **Pre-Flight Check First:** Start by verifying target environment (`uname -m`, proot/host, tool versions, free disk, or required env vars) before any mutating step.\n2. **Termux Copy-Paste Safe Steps:** Keep each step self-contained, short enough not to glitch mobile terminal buffers, and newline-safe (`&&` / `;`). Never chain >3 unrelated phases blindly.\n3. **Verify & Recover Every Step:** Pair each step with one observable success signal (exit `0`, expected stdout, `diff -s`, HTTP `200`, or file check) plus the exact 1-line recovery command for common blockers (`LD_PRELOAD`, missing lib, DNS, permission denied, port in use).\n\n## Invariants\n- **NEVER** emit destructive commands (`rm -rf`, overwrite, force-push) without a backup/dry-run warning and explicit target path check.\n- **NEVER** leave unverified `<placeholder>` flags inside runnable commands without flagging them clearly up front.\n",
