    kind: "skill",
    tags: ['skill', 'library'],
    content: "---\nname: writing-for-agents\ndescription: Author dense, V6-standard AGENTS.md and SKILL.md modules (<=30 lines, <=140-char descriptions, lazy-load, hard verification gates).\nwhen_not_to_use: User-facing README.md docs (use readme-craft) or application source code.\nverified: \"2026-11\"\ntriggers: [author skill.md, write agents.md, compress prompt, frontmatter]\n---\n# Writing For Agents (v6 · V6 Skill Standard)\n\n## Must-do\n1. **V6 Density & Frontmatter:** Keep every `SKILL.md` `<=30` lines (`16-28` ideal) and `description <=140` chars packed with exact trigger nouns/symptoms. Always include `name`, `description`, `when_not_to_use`, `verified`, and `triggers`.\n2. **Lazy-Load & Context Discipline:** Whenever `assets` (`references/*`, `scripts/*`) exist, add an explicit `> **Lazy-load:**` rule so agents skip reading them on routine tasks. Protect `100K` context (no raw lockfile/log dumps; route heavy scans to subagents).\n3. **Actionable Body:** Use imperative sections (`Must-do`, `Verification Gate`, `Invariants`) with exact paths, runnable checks, and zero fabricated metrics/broken probes.\n4. **Sync & Lean `AGENTS.md`:** Save under `/root/workspaces/opencode-skills/<name>/SKILL.md`, sync to `/root/.config/opencode/skills/<name>/SKILL.md`, and verify `diff -s`. Never bloat `AGENTS.md` with per-skill indices.\n\n## Invariants\n- **NEVER** include filler intros, vague advice (\"write clean code\"), stale paths, unverified versions, or emoji in agent specs.\n- **Verification Gate:** Confirm `wc -l <= 30`, `description <= 140` chars, and `diff -s` (`are identical`) across both skill directories.\n",
